                <pb facs="0881" n="782" sameAs="frus:frus1936v02/pg782"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">852.00/4061: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Portugal</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Caldwell</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Lisbon</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-12-11T11:00:00+00:00">December 11, 1936—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 11—8:20 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>74. Note just received from Spanish insurgent representative here states that
                    vessels navigating at night without lights in Spanish waters will be considered
                    enemy vessels.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Caldwell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
